{"name":"Black Truffle","hex":"#463d3e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black truffle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A species of truffle, Tuber melanosporum, darker than the white truffle, most commonly from France but also found in other parts of Europe, that is prized as a culinary ingredient."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black_truffle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tuber melanosporum","blocks":[{"text":"Tuber melanosporum, commonly called black truffle, Périgord truffle or French black truffle, is a species of truffle native to Southern Europe. It is one of the most expensive edible fungi in the world. In 2013, the truffle cost between 1,000 and 2,000 euros per kilogram."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Truffe_nature.JPG/330px-Truffe_nature.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuber_melanosporum"},{"title":"Truffle","blocks":[{"text":"A truffle is the fruiting body of a subterranean ascomycete fungus, one of the species of the genus Tuber. More than one hundred other genera of fungi are classified as truffles including Geopora, Peziza, Choiromyces, and Leucangium. These genera belong to the class Pezizomycetes and the Pezizales order. Several truffle-like basidiomycetes are excluded from Pezizales, including Rhizopogon and Glomus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Truffe_noire_du_P%C3%A9rigord.jpg/330px-Truffe_noire_du_P%C3%A9rigord.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truffle"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Truffi%C3%A8re_des_Gr%C3%A8zes_01.jpg/500px-Truffi%C3%A8re_des_Gr%C3%A8zes_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Truffi%C3%A8re_des_Gr%C3%A8zes_01.jpg/500px-Truffi%C3%A8re_des_Gr%C3%A8zes_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Black truffle, cut","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATruffi%C3%A8re_des_Gr%C3%A8zes_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Beaumont_-_truffi%C3%A8res.jpg/500px-Beaumont_-_truffi%C3%A8res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Beaumont_-_truffi%C3%A8res.jpg/1280px-Beaumont_-_truffi%C3%A8res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Beaumont_-_truffi%C3%A8res.jpg/500px-Beaumont_-_truffi%C3%A8res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Black truffles suppress the growth of plants around their symbiont, creating the impression of a burnt area.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeaumont_-_truffi%C3%A8res.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/White_truffles_from_San_Miniato.jpg/500px-White_truff